WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:02.370
- Welcome back everybody.

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:05.040
We've got the legendary
Carol Burnett with us.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.068
Give it up.

00:00:06.068 --> 00:00:07.989
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.989 --> 00:00:09.540
So let's finish things up here

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.610
with something Carol
liked to do on her show

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.320
and her comedy specials, which we love,

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.286
which is take questions from the audience.

00:00:15.286 --> 00:00:16.890
All right, let's turn to our audience

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.000
for their questions right now.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.770
So who has a question for Carol?

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:20.939
Oh, everybody has a question for Carol.

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:23.430
All right, well I'm just,
do you, we wanna pick?

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:24.263
Do I wanna pick?

00:00:24.263 --> 00:00:25.770
I get to pick, I'm gonna pick
you right here in the blue,

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:26.856
how about that?

00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:28.350
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.030
- Hi Carol.
- [Carol] Hi.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.910
- In the 90 years that
you've been on this planet,

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:33.780
what would you say is the

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.060
most important thing you've learned?

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.890
- Oh, that's a big question.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.900
- Do you have about 40 hours?

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.510
(audience laughing)

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.910
Not to take yourself too seriously.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.100
- Not to take yourself too
seriously, okay, check.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.630
Okay, I'm gonna go with
orange, back there,

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.600
yeah, with the cool red hair, come on now.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.444
- Hi, outside of entertainment,

00:00:54.444 --> 00:00:58.080
what do you still want to
accomplish in your life?

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:58.913
- Ooh, outside of entertainment,

00:00:58.913 --> 00:01:00.960
what do you want to accomplish?

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:01.980
- George Clooney.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:05.063
(audience laughing)

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.371
- Oh my God.

00:01:14.122 --> 00:01:17.747
That's my favorite part
of this whole show.

00:01:17.747 --> 00:01:19.290
Oh, anyway.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.390
So who else has a question for Carol?

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.650
That was amazing.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.330
Okay, I'm gonna go blue down here.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:25.800
Blue jacket, okay.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.750
- Carol, this is amazing to be so close

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.890
to a legend like you.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.161
I think we're all thrilled,
but could you tell us

00:01:31.161 --> 00:01:35.100
where did your famous
Tarzan yell come from?

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.503
- Well, I had a beautiful cousin,

00:01:37.503 --> 00:01:40.080
we were the same age and around nine,

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.951
10 years old, we used to
go to the movies together

00:01:42.951 --> 00:01:45.240
and she was beautiful.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.172
I mean, she looked like
a baby Sharon Stone,

00:01:47.172 --> 00:01:49.050
I mean, just gorgeous.
- Yeah.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:52.383
- And so when we would see
a movie with Nelson Eddy

00:01:52.383 --> 00:01:55.551
and Jeanette MacDonald, we'd
come home and play them.

00:01:55.551 --> 00:01:58.530
And of course, she'd be Jeanette and guess

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.753
who would be Nelson.

00:01:59.753 --> 00:02:00.930
(audience laughing)

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.501
So when we saw Tarzan and Jane,

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:07.023
it was either my being
Tarzan or the monkey.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.620
Or a cheetah, because she was always Jane.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.920
So I taught myself how
to do the Tarzan yell

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.510
when I was about nine or 10.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.404
It's a yodel.

00:02:16.404 --> 00:02:17.237
- Oh which I love.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.350
- Goes from head to chest,
head to chest, head.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:20.183
- Yeah.

00:02:20.183 --> 00:02:24.480
- I taught that to Beverly
Sills, the opera singer.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.313
- Yes.

00:02:25.313 --> 00:02:26.970
- When we did a special
years ago together,

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.520
called "Sills and Burnett at the Met."

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:33.360
And Beverly said, "How do
you do that Tarzan thing?"

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.520
And I showed it and she did it.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.985
And of course she did it beautifully.

00:02:36.985 --> 00:02:40.590
And she said, "You know,
it's a great vocal exercise."

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:44.192
- Yeah, I just love that you
got an opera singer to yodel.

00:02:44.192 --> 00:02:45.025
- I know.

00:02:45.025 --> 00:02:45.890
- It's like, that's amazing,

00:02:46.863 --> 00:02:48.390
I'm like, you never hear that.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.430
- So, okay, well it
has been such an honor.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:51.360
Thank you guys for the questions.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.650
Those were awesome questions.
- Thank you.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.320
- George Clooney answer, wins the day.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.083
I just have one last thing to say, Jason?

00:03:05.617 --> 00:03:10.617
♪ I'm so glad we had this time together ♪

00:03:12.287 --> 00:03:17.287
♪ Just to have a laugh or sing a song ♪

00:03:19.286 --> 00:03:24.286
♪ Seems we just get started
and before you know it ♪

00:03:26.106 --> 00:03:30.773
♪ Comes the time we have to say so long ♪

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:33.557
We got one more verse.

00:03:33.557 --> 00:03:38.557
♪ There's a time you
put aside for dreaming ♪

00:03:40.317 --> 00:03:45.317
♪ And a time for things you have to do ♪

00:03:47.171 --> 00:03:52.171
♪ But the time I like the
best is in the evening ♪

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:58.657
♪ I can spend a moment here with you ♪

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:05.701
(audience cheering)

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:06.672
- You're a doll.

00:04:06.672 --> 00:04:09.922
- That was my way of sliding in a duet.

00:04:11.466 --> 00:04:13.123
Carol Burnett, everybody.

00:04:13.123 --> 00:04:16.123
(audience cheering)

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.867
Okay, you can see "Carol Burnett, 90 Years

00:04:19.867 --> 00:04:21.810
"of Laughter and Love," tonight on NBC.

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:23.973
You do not wanna miss it, it's amazing.

